course: dictionary
lesson: 6057
title: Meow: a sound, a word, a joke
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A meow is the soft crying sound a cat makes. «The cat meowed all night and Mum was cross.» Here meowed is a verb: it tells you what the cat did.
explain: Meow is a sound word, called onomatopoeia, because it sounds like the noise it names. Cats meow mostly to people, to ask for food or to be let in. «Your cat meowing at the fridge door is talking to you.»
explain: Meow can also be a noun: «a little meow» means one small cry. You can even shout «Meow!» on its own, which is called an interjection.
explain: Be careful with the slang. Sometimes people say "meow" after someone makes a catty, spiteful remark, as a joke. It has nothing to do with a real cat, so read the sentence to see which meaning fits.
fact: Meow is a verb, a noun and an interjection.
fact: The verb forms are meow, meows, meowed and meowing.
fact: «Meow» means the soft crying sound a cat makes.
fact: Adult cats rarely meow to each other; they meow mostly to people.
fact: Each cat can develop its own meows for its own family.
exercise: «The cat meowed all night and Mum was cross.» What does meowed mean here? | Ate all of its food | Ran fast across the garden | *Made the soft crying sound of a cat | Slept very deeply
exercise: Dad says, «Your cat is meowing at the fridge door.» Why is the cat meowing? | It wants to sing a song for the fridge | It is playing a game of hide and seek | It is talking to the cat next door | *It is trying to talk to you, perhaps asking for food
exercise: Which sentence uses meow as a noun, meaning one small sound? | The cat is meowing loudly. | *I heard a little meow from under the bed. | Please meow for me. | The cat meows at the door.
test: «Adult cats rarely meow to each other.» Who do cats mostly meow to? | *People | Birds | Other cats | Dogs
test: Which form fits? «The kitten was ___ at the window all morning.» | *meowing | meows | meow | meowed
exam: Jade's friend makes a spiteful remark, and Jade just says "Meow" as a joke. What does Jade mean? | *She is making a slang joke about the catty remark | Hello, little cat | The cat is hungry | Meow is a noun meaning a bed
